{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":16829511,"ns":0,"title":"Beauville–Laszlo theorem","extract":"In mathematics, the Beauville–Laszlo theorem is a result in commutative algebra and algebraic geometry that allows one to \"glue\" two sheaves over an infinitesimal neighborhood of a point on an algebraic curve.  It was proved by Arnaud Beauville and Yves Laszlo (1995).","description":"Lets one glue 2 sheaves over an infinitesimal neighborhood of an algebraic curve point","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}